# Two Trait Doctorings encoded on Llanowar Elves (CR 702.99): each exiled card gives the creature its own ability, so when the
# Elves deal combat damage there are two triggers and each one, resolving, copies and casts its own encoded card. A copy of
# a cipher spell is not represented by a card, so it is not encoded (CR 702.99a): when the copies resolve nothing is asked
# about a creature to encode them on (`! Bot1.Choose`, though the Elves are a creature Bot1 controls), they cease to exist
# (CR 707.10), and the two cards are still exiled, still encoded. The first copy changes a basic land type, the second
# a color word. Trait Doctoring has no word to change in Llanowar Elves, whose text is only a mana symbol, and that is no
# reason not to target it (the ruling: any permanent may be targeted); both are encoded on it as they resolve.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Island
Island
Trait Doctoring
Trait Doctoring
Forest
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Trait Doctoring.Cast(Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Modes(Replace a color word)
Bot1.Colors(Green)
Bot1.Colors(Blue)
Bot1.Choose(Llanowar Elves)
? Exile = Trait Doctoring
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Trait Doctoring.Cast(Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Modes(Replace a color word)
Bot1.Colors(Green)
Bot1.Colors(Blue)
Bot1.Choose(Llanowar Elves)
? Exile.Count = 2
Bot1.Attack(Llanowar Elves)
[T5 Bot1.CombatDamage]
Bot1.Triggers(Llanowar Elves; Llanowar Elves)
? Stack.Count = 2
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Island)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Modes(Replace a basic land type)
Bot1.Modes(Island)
Bot1.Modes(Swamp)
! Bot1.Choose
? Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Subtypes = Swamp
? Exile.Count = 2
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Island)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Modes(Replace a color word)
Bot1.Colors(Blue)
Bot1.Colors(Red)
! Bot1.Choose
? Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Colors = (absent)
? Stack.Count = 0

